# Helm as a Finder replacement: feature parity catalogue (02-finder-parity)

Author: Fable 5.1 (architecture lead). Inputs read in full: `00-current-state.md` (with Appendix C errata, which wins on conflict), `00b-opus-review.md`, `00a-astra-first-pass.md`, and the module list, access policy and deferred-feature seams of `01-architecture.md`. Source spot-checked where a row depends on actual behaviour: `App/Info.plist` (Helm already registers `public.folder` as an Alternate Viewer), `Models/FileItem.swift` (prefetch keys; no alias, tag, dataless or quarantine keys), `Models/Place.swift` (Trash is the literal `~/.Trash`; `network` kind exists but is never instantiated).

## 0. How to read this document

**Scope.** Every user-visible Finder capability on macOS 14 that a personal power user could notice is missing, grouped by area, plus the macOS integration questions that decide whether "replacement" is even possible. The catalogue is deliberately exhaustive (several hundred rows) so that later phases can pick from it rather than rediscover it.

**Columns.**

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| ID | `P-nnn`, stable, cited by later phases. |
| Item | Short name. |
| What Finder does | The exact observable behaviour, including shortcut, as a target to match or consciously deviate from. |
| Helm today | `Yes`, `Partial`, `No`, citing `F-xxx` (features) and `B-xxx` (bugs) from the Phase 0 audit and `M-xx`/`C-xx` from the Opus review. "Yes" means reachable and roughly right, not bug-free. |
| Pri | `P0` must-have for a daily-driver replacement; `P1` important, expected within the first year; `P2` nice-to-have, parity for completeness, or consciously deferred. |
| Cx | Build complexity under the blind-authoring constraint: `S` under a day of model work, `M` a few days, `L` a week or more, `XL` a multi-week subsystem or one that needs real-Mac iteration. |
| APIs | macOS APIs involved. Only public, documented, macOS 14-available APIs are listed; private ones are named only to say they must not be used. |
| Modules | Where the work lands in the `01-architecture` package: `Core` (`HelmCore`), `FS` (`HelmFileSystem`), `Ops` (`HelmOperations`), `Search` (`HelmSearch`), `Persist` (`HelmPersistence`), `UI` (`HelmUI`), `App` (`HelmApp`). |
| Notes / pitfalls | What will bite, what to verify on a Mac, and where Helm should deliberately differ. |

**Priority rule of thumb.** P0 is "I would go back to Finder within a day without it". P1 is "I would go back within a month". P2 is "I would shrug".

**Uncertainty.** Anything about macOS runtime behaviour that I could not confirm from documentation I remember with confidence is marked `[Needs verification on macOS]`. The Helm-side facts come from the audited source and are not marked.

**Helm identity constraints (from the audit §4.7 and 00b §5.5)** that this catalogue respects rather than overrides: Cmd+L typed-path address bar, explicit Cut/Paste that moves, Cmd+D toggles Star, Starred and Recent as first-class Places, `~/Templates` New File, grid and list as the primary views, batch rename modes, "Properties" naming, always-visible status bar. Where Finder parity conflicts with one of these, the row says so and proposes an alias or a setting rather than a silent replacement.

---

## 1. Windows, tabs and navigation

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-001 | Multiple windows | ⌘N opens a new window at the "New Finder windows show" location, cascaded from the last window; each window has its own history, view and selection. | Partial (F-001, F-003; M-03: `center()` defeats autosave and cascading; B-103 cold-open creates two windows) | P0 | S | `NSWindowController`, `NSWindow.cascadeTopLeft(from:)`, `setFrameAutosaveName` before `center()` is never called | App, UI | Cascade only the second and later windows; restore the saved frame for the first. |
| P-002 | Window tabs | ⌘T opens a tab (per the "Open folders in tabs" setting), native tab bar with close buttons, overflow, ⇧⌘T shows/hides the bar even with one tab. | Partial (F-009, F-010: custom 30 pt strip, hidden with one tab; B-020 toolbar state leaks; B-081 rebuild on every navigation) | P0 | L | `NSWindow.tabbingMode`, `tabbingIdentifier`, `NSWindowTabGroup`, `addTabbedWindow(_:ordered:)` | UI, App | Decision: native `NSWindow` tabs give drag-between-windows, Merge All Windows, VoiceOver and ⌃Tab for free, at the cost of one window per tab (toolbar and sidebar per tab). Custom strip keeps today's look but every parity row below it (P-003 to P-005) is then hand-built. Recommend native tabs with `tabbingMode = .preferred`. |
| P-003 | Tabs between windows | Drag a tab out to tear off a window, drag it into another window's bar, Window > Merge All Windows, Move Tab to New Window. | No | P1 | M | Native tab group gives this free; custom strip needs `NSDraggingSession` plus window re-parenting | UI | With a custom strip this becomes XL. |
| P-004 | Keyboard tab switching | ⌃Tab / ⌃⇧Tab cycle, ⇧⌘[ / ⇧⌘] previous/next, ⌘1..9 are view switches in Finder (not tab numbers). | No (F-010; audit §2.7 "not bound anywhere") | P0 | S | `NSWindow.selectNextTab(_:)`, `selectPreviousTab(_:)` with native tabs | UI | Keep ⌘1/⌘2 as view switches as today. |
| P-005 | Tab reorder and overflow | Drag to reorder; overflow collapses with a disclosure menu. | No (F-010; B-062 equal-width, no overflow) | P1 | M | Native tab bar | UI | Free with native tabs. |
| P-006 | Open in new tab / window | ⌘-double-click opens a folder in a new tab (or window per setting), ⌥-double-click opens in a new window and closes the old one, context menu "Open in New Tab" / "Open in New Window". | No | P1 | S | Modifier flags on the open action | UI, Core | The reducer already has "new tab inherits location" (F-009); add a target parameter. |
| P-007 | Close semantics | ⌘W closes the tab (window if last), ⇧⌘W closes the window with all tabs, ⌥⌘W closes all windows; closing a window with tabs prompts nothing. | Partial (F-011; M-05 no Close Window command) | P1 | S | Standard `performClose(_:)` | UI | Consider "Reopen Closed Tab" (⇧⌘T in browsers) as a Helm extra; Finder lacks it. |
| P-008 | Back / Forward | ⌘[ / ⌘] per tab; buttons disabled at the ends; click-and-hold the Back button shows a history menu. | Partial (F-005; B-019 duplicates and gaps; B-075 never disabled) | P0 | M | `NSToolbarItem` validation, `NSMenu` on press-and-hold via `NSSegmentedControl` or `NSButton` with a delayed menu | UI, Core | History model lives in `HelmCore.NavigationHistory`; dedupe same-location pushes; selection snapshots must be applied back to widgets (B-011). |
| P-009 | Enclosing folder and open | ⌘↑ goes up (at `/` stays), ⌘↓ opens the selection, ⌃⌘↑ opens the enclosing folder in a new window, ⌘O opens. | Partial (F-006; C-07 root guard probably wrong; ⌘↓/⌘O unbound) | P0 | S | Menu key equivalents | UI, Core | Up at a volume root should go to Computer (P-019), not `/`. |
| P-010 | Go menu locations | Recents ⇧⌘F, Documents ⇧⌘O, Desktop ⇧⌘D, Downloads ⌥⌘L, Home ⇧⌘H, Computer ⇧⌘C, AirDrop ⇧⌘R, Network ⇧⌘K, iCloud Drive ⇧⌘I, Applications ⇧⌘A, Utilities ⇧⌘U; holding ⌥ adds Library. | Partial (only Home ⇧⌘H, F-006) | P0 | S | `FileManager.urls(for:in:)`, `NSMenu` with ⌥ alternate items | UI, Core | Trivial wiring once Places exist; Network/AirDrop rows point at P-215 and P-291. |
| P-011 | Go to Folder | ⇧⌘G opens a floating panel: typed path, Tab completion, `~` expansion, recent paths, Return navigates; Ventura+ shows suggestions as you type. | Yes, as Helm's ⌘L address editor (F-014 to F-024; B-050 main-thread I/O, B-052 stale row on Return, B-054 files suggested but not committable) | P0 | M | `NSTextField` field editor, `NSPanel` | UI, FS, Core | Keep Helm's contract (00b §5.5 item 1); add ⇧⌘G as an alias that focuses the same editor; move completion into `HelmFileSystem.CompletionProvider` with request generations. |
| P-012 | Recent Folders menu | Go > Recent Folders lists the last ten folders with Clear Menu. | Partial (F-030 Recent place mixes files and folders) | P1 | S | `NSMenu` built from `RecentStore` | UI, Persist | Reuse the 300-record log; filter to directories. |
| P-013 | Session and window restoration | Windows, tabs, locations, view style, scroll and selection come back after relaunch and after "Reopen windows when logging back in". | No (F-068; C-06 position not even restored) | P0 | M | `NSWindowRestoration`, `NSWindow.restorationClass`, `encodeRestorableState(with:)`, or a Helm `SessionStore` written on change | App, Persist, UI | 01-architecture §10.3 chooses an own `SessionStore`; still adopt `NSApplication` secure restorable state so the system "reopen at login" flow works. Replace unmounted locations with Home and say so. |
| P-014 | Per-folder window frame memory | When "open in new window" mode is on, each folder remembers its window size and position (stored in that folder's `.DS_Store`). | No | P2 | M | Own store keyed by canonical path; `.DS_Store` is not readable (see P-061) | Persist, UI | Low value for a tabs-first user. |
| P-015 | Window title and proxy icon | Title is the folder name with its icon; ⌘-click the title shows the ancestor path menu; the proxy icon can be dragged as the folder. | No (F-072, M-04: title "Helm", hidden) | P0 | S | `NSWindow.representedURL`, `title`, `titleVisibility`; AppKit draws the proxy and path menu automatically from `representedURL` | UI | Helm hides the title bar today; with a unified toolbar the proxy still appears in the toolbar leading area when `titleVisibility = .visible`. Keep breadcrumb as the primary path. |
| P-016 | Window menu and cycling | Window menu lists windows with checkmark, ⌘` cycles, Minimize ⌘M, Zoom, full screen (green button). | Partial (F-066) | P1 | S | Standard `NSWindow` behaviour once titles are set | UI | Distinct titles (P-015) are what make this useful. |
| P-017 | New-window default location | Finder Settings > General "New Finder windows show": Recents, Home, Desktop, Documents, iCloud Drive, or any folder. | No (first tab always Home, B-018; `helm.defaultViewMode` style stubs B-059) | P1 | S | Settings model | Persist, UI | Also used for the Dock click when no windows are open. |
| P-018 | Opening folders from outside | `open <dir>`, Dock-icon drop, Services, and `NSWorkspace.open` on a folder bring the folder up in the key window or a new window; `application(_:openFiles:)` replies. | Partial (F-002; B-018 initial URL lost; B-103 two windows on cold open; B-114 no reply) | P0 | S | `NSApplicationDelegate.application(_:open:)`, `NSApplication.reply(toOpenOrPrint:)`, `OpenRequestRouter` buffering until launch completes | App | Decide target policy: key window new tab, unless the folder is already open in a tab (then select it). |
| P-019 | Computer location | ⇧⌘C shows all mounted volumes plus Network as a browsable root. | No | P1 | M | `FileManager.mountedVolumeURLs`, `NSWorkspace` mount notifications | Core, FS, UI | Needs the virtual-location model (01-architecture §5.6). Also the natural parent of a volume root for ⌘↑. |
| P-020 | Breadcrumb ancestor click | Not a Finder feature in the toolbar (Finder's path bar is at the bottom, P-261), but Helm's README promises ancestor navigation by click. | Partial (F-013; B-051 every click edits) | P0 | S | Button actions | UI | 01-architecture Q1 default: click navigates; current segment, empty space, ⌥-click and ⌘L edit. |
| P-021 | Keyboard focus model | The file pane has focus after launch, tab switch and view switch; Tab moves focus between sidebar, content and search when Full Keyboard Access is on. | No (B-102, F-071; B-108 editor traps ⌘F) | P0 | M | `NSWindow.initialFirstResponder`, `makeFirstResponder`, key-view loop (`nextKeyView`) | UI | 01-architecture §8.5 defines the focus model; treat programmatic focus moves as intentional. |
| P-022 | Show/hide chrome | View menu: Sidebar ⌥⌘S, Toolbar ⌥⌘T, Path Bar ⌥⌘P, Status Bar ⌘/, Tab Bar ⇧⌘T, Preview ⇧⌘P, each with checkmark. | Partial (sidebar only, as ⌃⌘S, F-004; status bar always on, F-064) | P1 | S | `NSSplitViewItem.isCollapsed`, `NSToolbar.isVisible` | UI | Keep ⌃⌘S working as a Helm alias; add ⌥⌘S for muscle memory. |
| P-023 | Spring-to-tab | Hovering a dragged item over a tab switches to it after a delay so the drop can land inside. | No | P2 | S | `NSDraggingDestination` on the tab bar (native tabs do this automatically) | UI | Free with native tabs. |
| P-024 | Show enclosing folder of a result | In search results and Recents, ⌘R (Show Original is replaced by "Show in Enclosing Folder") and the path bar reveal the item's folder with it selected. | Partial (F-050 "Show in Enclosing Folder" opens Finder, not Helm) | P0 | S | Navigate to parent, select item by identity | UI, Core | Helm must reveal in Helm. Keep "Reveal in Finder" as a separate command (P-316). |
| P-025 | Dual pane in one window | Not a Finder feature. | No (README's "dual-pane" means sidebar plus content) | P2 | L | Two `ContentHostController`s in an `NSSplitView` | UI | Beyond parity; 01-architecture lists "per-tab split panes" as a deferred seam. Listed so it is not forgotten. |
| P-026 | Loading, empty and denied states | A spinner while listing, "No items" in empty folders, "The folder X can't be opened because you don't have permission" with the window staying put, and the item count in the status bar. | No (B-017 errors look like empty folders; B-109 Trash blank without Full Disk Access) | P0 | M | `NSProgressIndicator`, `SnapshotPhase` in Core, Privacy pane URL `x-apple.systempreferences:com.apple.preference.security?Privacy_AllFiles` | Core, UI | A denied load must not enter history or Recent (01-architecture §9). |

## 2. Views

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-027 | Icon size | 16 to 512 pt via the status-bar slider and View Options, per folder, live. | Partial (F-035 fixed 96 pt; `helm.gridIconSize` stub, B-059) | P0 | M | `NSCollectionViewFlowLayout.itemSize`, `invalidateLayout`, `NSSlider` in the status bar | UI, Core | Re-request thumbnails at the new pixel size (P-054); size is part of the per-folder view state (P-060). |
| P-028 | Grid spacing | View Options slider for spacing between icons. | No | P1 | S | `minimumInteritemSpacing`, `minimumLineSpacing` | UI | Part of view state. |
| P-029 | Label text size | 10 to 16 pt per view. | No (fixed 11 pt grid, 13/12 pt list) | P1 | S | Cell fonts from view state | UI | |
| P-030 | Label position | Bottom (default) or right of the icon. | No | P2 | M | Two item-view layouts | UI | Low value. |
| P-031 | Show item info | A second grey line under the name: image dimensions, folder item count, audio duration, volume free space. | No | P2 | M | `MDItem` attributes (`kMDItemPixelWidth`, `kMDItemDurationSeconds`), directory child count | FS, UI | Child counts on network volumes are expensive; compute lazily and cache per change token. |
| P-032 | Show icon preview | Toggle between generic type icons and content thumbnails, per view. | Partial (F-048 thumbnails always on for eligible types) | P1 | S | Flag in view state consulted by the imaging pipeline | UI | |
| P-033 | Folder background | View Options: white, colour, or picture, per folder, icon view only. | No | P2 | S | `NSCollectionView.backgroundColors` / background view | UI, Persist | Per-folder store. |
| P-034 | Free-form icon placement | In icon view with Sort By None, icons sit where you drop them; positions persist in `.DS_Store`; Clean Up and Snap to Grid tidy them. | No (flow layout only) | P2 | XL | Custom `NSCollectionViewLayout` with per-item frames; own position store | UI, Persist | Recommend not building: the stored positions live in `.DS_Store`, which Helm will neither read reliably nor write (P-061), so Finder and Helm would disagree. Grid-only is a legitimate Nautilus-style choice. |
| P-035 | Icon labels | Two lines, middle truncation on the second line, full name on hover tooltip, selected label gets a rounded highlight. | Partial (F-035; M-19 probably renders one line) | P0 | S | `NSTextField.maximumNumberOfLines = 2`, `lineBreakMode = .byTruncatingMiddle`, `toolTip` | UI | Verify on macOS (01-architecture §14.2); fall back to tail truncation if middle plus wrapping misbehaves. |
| P-036 | List view columns | Name, Date Modified, Date Created, Date Last Opened, Date Added, Size, Kind, Version, Comments, Tags; Name is fixed first. | Partial (F-036: Name, Size, Date Modified, Kind) | P0 | M | `NSTableColumn` per key; `URLResourceKey.addedToDirectoryDateKey`, `creationDateKey`; `MDItem` for last-opened, version, comments | UI, FS, Core | Keep the column set in `HelmCore.ListColumn` so sort keys and columns share one enum. |
| P-037 | Column management | Right-click a header to show/hide columns; drag to resize and reorder; widths and order persist per view; "Use as Defaults". | No (B-078 no autosave) | P0 | S | `NSTableView.autosaveName`, `autosaveTableColumns`, header `NSMenu` | UI | Autosave per folder is a Helm store concern; AppKit autosave is global. |
| P-038 | Header-click sorting | Click a header to sort, click again to flip, indicator arrow shown. | No (B-034 headers unwired; B-035 descending comparator invalid) | P0 | S | `tableView(_:sortDescriptorsDidChange:)`, `NSSortDescriptor` prototypes | UI, Core | Sorting itself lives in `HelmCore.SortDescriptor`; the delegate only dispatches an action. |
| P-039 | Disclosure triangles | Folders expand inline; ⌥-click expands all descendants; → / ← expand/collapse; ⌥→ expands recursively; expanded children obey the same sort, hidden setting and selection commands. | Partial (F-037; B-032 child loads ignore settings; B-033 commands drop nested selection) | P0 | M | `NSOutlineView` with a `TreeSnapshot` of stable node identities | UI, Core, FS | Opus M-21: boxed structs may break `reloadItem` identity; use reference-type node wrappers keyed by `ItemID`. |
| P-040 | Calculate all sizes | View Options checkbox; folder sizes computed in the background and shown in the Size column; Get Info also totals. | No (C-22 folders show "Zero KB") | P1 | M | Background enumeration with `.totalFileAllocatedSizeKey`; cancel on navigation | FS, UI | Cache by directory change token; show a spinner glyph while computing. |
| P-041 | Relative dates | "Today at 09:12", "Yesterday", weekday for the last week, then the date; toggle "Use relative dates". | No | P1 | S | `DateFormatter.doesRelativeDateFormatting`, `RelativeDateTimeFormatter` | UI, Core | Formatting is pure logic; put it in Core for tests. |
| P-042 | List appearance options | Icon size small/large, text size, alternating row colours. | Partial (F-036 fixed 24 pt, alternating on) | P2 | S | `NSTableView.rowHeight`, `usesAlternatingRowBackgroundColors` | UI | |
| P-043 | Column view | ⌘3: side-by-side columns from the root, each column a list, the last column previews the selected file; → / ← move between columns; columns resize, ⌥-drag resizes all; "Show preview column" toggle. | No | P1 | XL | `NSBrowser` (public, old, works) or a horizontal `NSStackView` of `NSTableView`s; `QLPreviewView` for the preview column | UI, Core | 01-architecture keeps a `ContentWidget` seam. `NSBrowser` with `NSBrowserDelegate` item-based API is the least code; its cell-based past is irrelevant. Type-select and drag need per-column handling. |
| P-044 | Gallery view | ⌘4: a large preview of the selection above a horizontal thumbnail strip, with the metadata/preview pane on the right. | No | P2 | XL | `QLPreviewView`, horizontal `NSCollectionView` | UI | Build only after P-045 exists; it is mostly layout on top of it. |
| P-045 | Preview pane | ⇧⌘P shows a right-hand pane in any view: large preview, metadata (kind, size, dates, dimensions, tags), "Show More", and Quick Action buttons. | No | P1 | L | `QLPreviewView` (QuickLookUI), `MDItem` for metadata | UI, FS | Quick Actions in the pane are Finder-private (P-249); show Services and Share instead. |
| P-046 | View switching and defaults | ⌘1 icon, ⌘2 list, ⌘3 column, ⌘4 gallery, toolbar control; view style is per tab, remembered per folder, "Use as Defaults", "Always open in X view", "Browse in X view". | Partial (F-039 ⌘1/⌘2, tears down widgets; `helm.defaultViewMode` stub) | P0 | M | `ContentHostController` swapping `ContentWidget`s, per-folder view store | UI, Persist, Core | Keep widgets alive per tab so scroll and expansion survive (P-047). |
| P-047 | Preserve scroll, selection, expansion | Switching views and going Back restores selection and scroll position. | Partial (B-011 model-only selection; M-23 invisible selection acts) | P0 | S | Selection by `ItemID` applied after every snapshot commit | UI, Core | The single most dangerous current defect class; fix before anything else in this section. |
| P-048 | Large folders | 100k-item folders list in under a few seconds, scroll smoothly, sort without blocking. | No (B-010 sort per access; B-101 O(n² log n) selection; B-050 main-thread enumeration) | P0 | L | Streaming `FileManager.enumerator(at:includingPropertiesForKeys:options:)`, sorted immutable snapshot with `ItemID` index, diffable updates | FS, Core, UI | 01-architecture §5.4 and §12 budgets. Test with a synthetic 100k in-memory tree on Linux. |
| P-049 | Live updates | External adds, removes, renames appear within a second in every open view without losing selection or scroll; counts update. | No (B-009 stale widgets and crash; B-073 subtree noise; B-016 starvation) | P0 | M | FSEvents with path filtering, `NSCollectionView` / `NSOutlineView` batch updates from a diff | FS, Core, UI | Coalesce with a maximum latency (for example 250 ms debounce, 1 s cap). |
| P-050 | Item badges | Alias arrow badge, locked padlock, hidden items dimmed, cloud/download state, tag colour dots, shared-folder badge. | No (F-069 symlink flag unused) | P1 | M | `URLResourceKey.isAliasFileKey`, `isSymbolicLinkKey`, `isUserImmutableKey`, `tagNamesKey`, `ubiquitousItemDownloadingStatusKey`; badge composited onto the icon image | FS, UI | Composite badges at icon size; cache by (icon identity, badge set). |
| P-051 | Custom icons | Files and folders with a custom icon (Get Info paste, app bundles) show it. | Yes (F-047 `NSWorkspace.icon(forFile:)` returns custom icons) | P0 | S | `NSWorkspace.icon(forFile:)`, `NSWorkspace.setIcon(_:forFile:options:)` for setting | UI | Icon cache keys need a change token (B-056). |
| P-052 | Rubber-band selection | Drag on empty space selects by marquee in icon and list views. | Partial (`NSCollectionView` provides a marquee by default; `NSTableView` does not) | P1 | S | Custom marquee overlay for the list, or accept table-row drag selection | UI | Finder's list marquee is a nicety; P1. |
| P-053 | Name tooltips | Hovering a truncated name shows the full name. | No | P2 | S | `NSView.toolTip` | UI | |
| P-054 | Thumbnails everywhere | Content thumbnails in icon, list (small), column and gallery, at the exact display pixel size, refreshed when the file changes. | Partial (F-048; B-055 dropped subscribers; B-056 4× pixels, no invalidation) | P1 | S | `QLThumbnailGenerator` with `scale = backingScaleFactor`, cancel on reuse | UI, FS | Throttle concurrency (4 in flight) and skip network volumes unless requested. |

## 3. Sorting, grouping and view options

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-055 | Sort keys | View > Sort By: Name, Kind, Application, Date Last Opened, Date Added, Date Modified, Date Created, Size, Tags, None (icon view only). | Partial (F-040: name, size, date modified, kind) | P0 | M | `localizedStandardCompare`, `URLResourceKey.addedToDirectoryDateKey`, `creationDateKey`; `MDItemCopyAttribute(kMDItemLastUsedDate)`; default-app lookup for Application | Core, FS | Keys that need Spotlight metadata (last opened, application) must be fetched lazily and sorted with "unknown" last. |
| P-056 | Direction and tie-breaks | Ascending/descending with a strict weak order and a stable secondary key (name). | Partial (B-035 comparator negates equality) | P0 | S | Three-way comparison in `HelmCore.SortDescriptor` | Core | Unit-testable on Linux. |
| P-057 | Keep folders on top | Finder Settings > Advanced: "In windows when sorting by name" and "On Desktop"; off by default. | Partial (directories-first hard-coded true; `helm.directoriesFirst` stub) | P0 | S | Flag on the sort | Core, Persist | Helm's default of folders-first is the Nautilus choice; keep it default-on but honour the setting. |
| P-058 | Group by | View > Use Groups ⌃⌘0, then Group By (⌃⌘1 onward): None, Name, Kind, Application, Date Last Opened, Date Added, Date Modified, Date Created, Size, Tags. Date groups are Today, Yesterday, Previous 7 Days, Previous 30 Days, then months and years; size groups are buckets; each group has a header and its own sort. | No | P1 | L | Section headers in `NSCollectionViewFlowLayout` (`NSCollectionView.SupplementaryElementKind.sectionHeader`), group rows in `NSOutlineView` (`isGroupItem`) | Core, UI | Bucketing is pure logic in Core; the two widgets need section-aware data sources. |
| P-059 | Show View Options | ⌘J opens a floating panel bound to the front window's folder: always-open-in-view, group by, sort by, icon size, spacing, text size, label position, show item info, show icon preview, background, "Use as Defaults". | No (settings window has stubs, B-059) | P1 | M | `NSPanel` (utility, floating) with SwiftUI form | UI, Persist | Bind to the active tab's folder; changing tabs retargets the panel. |
| P-060 | Per-folder view settings | View style, sort, icon size and the rest persist per folder (Finder: `.DS_Store`) and fall back to defaults. | No | P1 | M | Own JSON store keyed by canonical path with a size cap; optional read-only `.DS_Store` parse | Persist, Core | Keep the store bounded (for example 5k folders, LRU). Reading `.DS_Store` is a community-documented private format; treat it as best-effort P2 (L) and never write it. |
| P-061 | `.DS_Store` policy | Finder writes `.DS_Store` in every folder it shows; it is hidden and ignored by other apps. | n/a | P0 | S | None | FS | Policy: never create, modify or delete `.DS_Store`; show it only when hidden files are shown; exclude it from "folder is empty" judgments and from item counts (Finder also excludes it). Writing it corrupts Finder state; deleting it loses Finder's icon positions. |
| P-062 | Date Added and Date Last Opened | Sort and columns for both. | No | P1 | M | `addedToDirectoryDateKey` (public); last opened via `MDItemCreate` + `kMDItemLastUsedDate` (requires indexing) | FS | Last-opened is unavailable on unindexed volumes; show "--". Helm's own Recent log can supplement. |
| P-063 | Natural, locale-aware name sort | "File 2" before "File 10"; diacritics and case folded per locale. | Yes (F-040 `localizedStandardCompare`) | P0 | S | `String.localizedStandardCompare` | Core | Not Linux-reproducible byte for byte; tests should assert relative order, not exact collation. |
| P-064 | Sort in virtual locations | Search results default to relevance (then any key), Recents default to Date Last Opened. | Partial (B-022 relevance destroyed; B-030 Recent re-sorted by name) | P0 | S | Per-location default sort in the snapshot | Core | Needs the `Location` model so each kind has its own default. |
| P-065 | Sort/Group controls | Toolbar "Group" (previously Arrange) popup and View > Sort By submenu with checkmarks, plus the list header. | No | P1 | S | `NSMenu` state from the active snapshot | UI | Also expose in the background context menu as Finder does. |
| P-066 | Clean Up / Snap to Grid | Icon view: Clean Up, Clean Up By (name, kind, …), Snap to Grid. | No | P2 | S | Only meaningful with P-034 | UI | With a flow layout the view is always "clean"; omit the commands rather than ship no-ops. |

## 4. Selection and keyboard navigation

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-067 | Type-select | Typing selects the first item whose name starts with the typed prefix, in every view; multi-character buffer with a short timeout; works on the sorted order. | Partial (F-041: list inherits `NSTableView` type-select; grid has none) | P0 | M | `NSTableViewDelegate.tableView(_:typeSelectStringFor:row:)`, custom `keyDown` buffer for `NSCollectionView` (`HelmCore.TypeSelect`) | Core, UI | The buffer and matching are pure logic in Core; the grid needs its own key handling. Space must not be swallowed by type-select (B-060). |
| P-068 | Arrow navigation | Icon view moves in two dimensions; list moves up/down; column moves across; Home/End, Page Up/Down scroll; ⌥↑/↓ jump to first/last. | Partial (grid arrows native; keys never reach the pane, B-102) | P0 | S | `NSCollectionView` / `NSTableView` default key handling once focused | UI | Mostly free after P-021. |
| P-069 | Selection gestures | Click selects, ⇧-click extends a range, ⌘-click toggles, ⇧↑/↓ extends, ⌘A selects all, clicking empty space deselects, marquee (P-052). | Partial (F-038; M-22 grid right-click bypasses delegate) | P0 | S | Native widget behaviour; `selectAll(_:)` forwarded to the pane | UI | Select All must target the pane, not the search field, unless the field is first responder. |
| P-070 | Open and navigate keys | ⌘↓ or ⌘O opens the selection (folders navigate in place), double-click the same, ⌘↑ goes up. | Partial (F-007 double-click; ⌘↓/⌘O unbound) | P0 | S | Menu key equivalents | UI | Multiple folders selected: Finder opens each in a new tab/window; Helm opens the last (F-070). Choose "each in a new tab". |
| P-071 | Rename in place | Return starts editing the name with the base name selected (extension excluded); Esc cancels; Tab commits and edits the next item; the field grows with the text; invalid names are refused with an explanation. | Partial (F-054 modal alert; B-046 no validation; B-066 preselection broken; B-118 Return without validation) | P0 | M | Editable `NSTextField` in the cell, `NSText` field editor, `FileNameValidator` in Core | UI, Core, Ops | Finder displays `/` as `:` and stores `:` as `/`; refuse `/` and `:` outright in Helm. Extension-change warning (P-363). Case-only rename on case-insensitive APFS: `FileManager.moveItem` may refuse; use `rename(2)` through the FS layer (00b R-18). |
| P-072 | Quick Look keys | Space toggles the panel, ⌥Space opens full screen, ⌘Y toggles too; arrows move the selection while the panel is open. | Partial (F-049; B-060 no modifier check, no reload on selection change; C-21 can preview an invisible selection) | P0 | S | `QLPreviewPanel`, `previewPanel(_:handle:)` to forward arrow keys | UI | See section 5. |
| P-073 | Delete keys | ⌘⌫ trashes, ⌥⌘⌫ deletes immediately with confirmation, ⇧⌘⌫ empties the Trash with confirmation, ⌥⇧⌘⌫ empties without confirmation. | Partial (⌘⌫ only, F-053; `confirmBeforeTrash` ignored, B-048) | P0 | S | Menu wiring onto the operations engine | UI, Ops | Delete Immediately needs its own confirmation text naming the count. |
| P-074 | Undo and redo | ⌘Z / ⇧⌘Z with named actions ("Undo Move of 3 Items"), covering move, copy, duplicate, rename, trash, put back, new folder; failures are reported, not swallowed. | Partial (F-059; B-041 permanent delete on undo, B-042 wrong names, B-043 no redo, B-100 freed target crash) | P0 | L | `NSUndoManager` bridge to the `OperationJournal` (01-architecture ADR-009) | Ops, UI | Undo of a copy must trash, never `removeItem`, and must verify identity (change token) first. |
| P-075 | Get Info keys | ⌘I opens one window per selected item (asks beyond 10), ⌥⌘I opens the single Inspector that follows the selection, ⌃⌘I opens Summary Info totalling a multi-selection. | Partial (F-050 single read-only sheet; B-117 sheet may not close) | P1 | M | `NSPanel` windows, `NSWindowController` per item | UI | Section 6 covers content. |
| P-076 | ⌘D | Finder: Duplicate. Helm: Toggle Star. | Partial (Helm's ⌘D is Star, F-029; Duplicate is unbound) | P0 | S | Key equivalents | UI | Decision: keep ⌘D = Star (Helm identity), bind Duplicate to ⇧⌘D with a settings switch "Finder-style ⌘D duplicates". Record in the keyboard contract. |
| P-077 | Remaining File/Edit/View/Go equivalents | ⌃⌘A Make Alias, ⌘R Show Original, ⌘E Eject, ⌘K Connect to Server, ⌃⌘N New Folder with Selection, ⌃⌘T Add to Sidebar, ⌥⌘C Copy as Pathname, ⌥⌘V Move Items Here, ⇧⌘. Toggle Hidden, ⌘J View Options, ⇧⌘G Go to Folder, ⌘P Print, ⌘F Find, ⇧⌘N New Folder, ⌘, Settings. | No for most (audit §2.7: only ⌘. for hidden, ⌘F, ⇧⌘N, ⌘, exist) | P0 | S | Menu construction; each item's command is its own row elsewhere | UI | Build the full menu bar first with disabled placeholders so validation and discoverability exist from day one. |
| P-078 | Menu and toolbar validation | Items disable with no selection or at history ends; checkmarks reflect state (hidden files, view, sort, sidebar). | No (B-075) | P0 | S | `NSMenuItemValidation.validateMenuItem(_:)`, `NSToolbarItemValidation` | UI | Validation reads the active snapshot only; never does I/O. |
| P-079 | Full Keyboard Access | With System Settings > Keyboard > Keyboard navigation on, Tab/⇧Tab move focus across sidebar, content, toolbar and search with visible focus rings; Esc leaves text fields. | No (B-061 editor traps Tab; B-108 ⌘F trap) | P1 | M | Key-view loop, `NSView.focusRingType`, `canBecomeKeyView` | UI | Address editor must release Tab when the completion popup is not showing a selectable row. |
| P-080 | Selection identity | Selection survives reload, rename of the selected item, sort change and external changes; renamed items stay selected under their new name. | No (B-011; B-009 index-based grid mapping) | P0 | M | `ItemID` (standardized path plus inode/file ID as change token) | Core, UI | Rename moves identity: map old to new ID in the reducer when Helm performed the rename; for external renames FSEvents gives old and new paths (`kFSEventStreamEventFlagItemRenamed` pairs) but pairing is heuristic. |
| P-081 | Tab selects next item | Legacy Finder behaviour: Tab / ⇧Tab select the next / previous item alphabetically when Full Keyboard Access is off. | No | P2 | S | `keyDown` in the pane | UI | Conflicts with P-079 when keyboard navigation is on; mirror Finder's conditional. |
| P-082 | Action (gear) menu | Toolbar Action item shows the context menu for the selection or folder. | No | P1 | S | `NSMenuToolbarItem` | UI | Also the keyboard route to the context menu for users who cannot right-click. |
| P-083 | Right-click semantics | Right-clicking an unselected item selects only it; on a selected item keeps the group; on the background clears. | Yes (F-038; M-22 grid path may leave the model stale) | P0 | S | `selectItems` plus explicit delegate notification | UI | Route all selection changes through one reducer action. |
| P-084 | Status text for selection | "3 of 120 selected, 2.1 GB" (total bytes of the selection), "120 items, 500 GB available". | Partial (F-064 count only) | P1 | S | `ByteCountFormatter`, `StatusText` in Core | Core, UI | Totals of folders use allocated size only when P-040 has computed them. |

