| P-087 | Multi-item preview | With several items selected, the panel shows arrows and an index-sheet button (grid of all items). | Partial (multiple `NSURL`s supplied) | P1 | S | Data source count/at index | UI | Free once the data source is right. |
| P-088 | Full screen and slideshow | ⌥Space opens the panel full screen; ⌥⌘Y runs a slideshow that auto-advances. | No | P2 | S | `QLPreviewPanel.enterFullScreenMode(_:withOptions:)` for full screen; auto-advance is not exposed | UI | Implement full screen; a timer that calls `currentPreviewItemIndex += 1` gives a plain slideshow `[Needs verification on macOS]` that the panel honours index changes while full screen. |
| P-089 | Panel actions | The panel's title bar offers "Open with X", Share, and Finder-only Quick Actions (Markup, Rotate, Trim, Create PDF). | Partial (Open and Share are provided by the panel itself) | P2 | S | None needed for Open/Share | UI | Quick Actions in the panel are Finder-private (see P-249); Services menu is the substitute. |
| P-090 | Keyboard while previewing | Arrow keys move the pane's selection while the panel is open; Esc closes; Space toggles. | No (no key forwarding) | P0 | S | `previewPanel(_:handle:)` returns false for arrows so the pane handles them, then `reloadData()` | UI | Without this the panel traps focus. |
| P-091 | Preview in virtual locations | Quick Look works in search results, Recents and Trash. | Partial (root items only, B-033) | P0 | S | Same data source over any snapshot | UI | Trash items need Full Disk Access to read (P-298). |
