| P-093 | Preview of cloud-only items | Previewing a dataless iCloud item downloads it first with a progress badge. | No | P2 | S | `FileManager.startDownloadingUbiquitousItem(at:)` before preview | FS, UI | Only iCloud has a public download call; other providers download on open (P-230). |

## 6. Get Info / inspector

Helm calls this "Properties" (F-050); the name stays, the content grows.

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-094 | Info window | ⌘I opens a resizable per-item window (not a sheet) with collapsible sections whose open/closed state persists; several items open several windows; beyond ten it asks. | Partial (F-050 fixed 360×480 modal sheet, read-only; B-117 Done may not dismiss) | P0 | L | `NSWindowController` + SwiftUI `Form` with `DisclosureGroup`; window per `ItemID` | UI, Persist | A window, not a sheet, so the user can keep browsing. Reuse an open window for the same item. |
| P-095 | General section | Kind, Size as "1.23 GB on disk (1,234,567,890 bytes) for 456 items" with a live recursive total, Where (clickable path), Created, Modified, Version (for bundles), Tags, Label. | Partial (F-050: size, parent path, dates, UTI; C-22 folder size "Zero KB"; `sizeInBytes` unused B-066) | P0 | M | `URLResourceValues` (`totalFileAllocatedSize`, `creationDate`, `contentModificationDate`), background enumeration for totals, `Bundle(url:)` for version | FS, UI | Totals are the same job as P-040; share the calculator and cancel when the window closes. |
| P-096 | Custom icon editing | Click the icon, paste an image or drag one on to set a custom icon; ⌫ restores the default. | No | P2 | M | `NSWorkspace.setIcon(_:forFile:options:)` (nil image removes) | UI, FS | Public API; writes the `Icon\r` resource and FinderInfo flag itself. |
| P-097 | Tags field | Token field listing tags with colour dots; typing adds; suggestions from the tag list. | No | P1 | M | `NSTokenField` or SwiftUI equivalent; tag store (section 9) | UI, FS | |
| P-098 | Stationery Pad | Checkbox; opening a stationery file creates an untitled copy in the app. | No | P2 | S | `com.apple.FinderInfo` xattr bit `kIsStationery` via `setxattr` | FS | The 32-byte FinderInfo layout is documented in the old Carbon `FileInfo` struct; writing it is safe if the existing 32 bytes are read-modify-written. Low value. |
| P-099 | Locked | Checkbox setting the user-immutable flag; locked items refuse rename/edit/trash until unlocked (P-129). | No | P1 | S | `URLResourceValues.isUserImmutable` (settable), equivalent to `chflags uchg` | FS, UI | Badge in views (P-050). |
| P-100 | Name & Extension | Editable name; "Hide extension" checkbox. | No | P1 | S | `URLResourceValues.hasHiddenExtension` (settable) | FS, UI | Display name must honour this everywhere (P-152). |
| P-101 | Comments | Editable Spotlight comment, searchable. | No | P2 | M | xattr `com.apple.metadata:kMDItemFinderComment` (binary plist string) via `setxattr`; read with `MDItem` or `getxattr` | FS, UI | Finder also mirrors comments into `.DS_Store`; whether Finder's Get Info shows a comment written only as the xattr `[Needs verification on macOS]`. Spotlight indexes the xattr, so search works regardless. |
| P-102 | More Info | Metadata section: dimensions, colour space, duration, codecs, camera, pages, authors, last opened, where from (download URL). | No (F-050 shows image dimensions only, read on the main thread B-058) | P1 | M | `MDItemCreate(kCFAllocatorDefault, path)` + `MDItemCopyAttributes`, `kMDItemWhereFroms`, `kMDItemLastUsedDate`; `CGImageSource` as fallback | FS, UI | Read off the main actor; attributes are absent on unindexed volumes. |
| P-103 | Open with | Popup of applications with the default marked; "Change All…" makes it the default for every file of that type. | Partial (F-050 shows the default app name only; `availableApplications` loaded but hidden) | P1 | M | `NSWorkspace.urlsForApplications(toOpen:)`, `urlForApplication(toOpen:)`, `setDefaultApplication(at:toOpenFileAt:completion:)` for this file, `setDefaultApplication(at:toOpen: UTType, completion:)` for Change All (all macOS 12+) | UI, FS | Per-file default is stored by Launch Services; no xattr hand-writing needed. |
| P-104 | Preview section | Live preview of the item inside the window. | No | P1 | S | `QLPreviewView` (QuickLookUI) with `previewItem` | UI | Shut down the view (`close()`) when the window closes to free the renderer. |
| P-105 | Sharing & Permissions | Table of owner, group, everyone (and ACL entries) with privilege popups (Read & Write, Read only, Write only, No Access), +/- to add users or groups (requires the lock/admin), "Apply to enclosed items…", "Make me the owner". | No (F-050 shows POSIX words read-only) | P1 | L | `FileManager.attributesOfItem` and `setAttributes([.posixPermissions])`, `acl_get_file`/`acl_set_file` (C, public), `getpwuid`/`getgrgid`, `OpenDirectory` to list users and groups | FS, UI | Owner changes and edits to files you do not own need root; Finder authenticates. Helm shows the controls disabled with "requires administrator" unless P-130 is built. ACL editing is error-prone; ship read-only ACL display first. |
| P-106 | Multi-item and Summary info | ⌃⌘I shows one window totalling the selection (count, total size); ⌘I with many items opens many windows; tag and lock edits in a multi-item window apply to all. | No | P2 | M | Same window with an aggregate model | UI | |
| P-107 | Inspector | ⌥⌘I opens one floating panel that updates as the selection changes. | No | P1 | M | `NSPanel` (`.utilityWindow`, `hidesOnDeactivate = false`) bound to the active tab's selection | UI | Same content as P-094 with a different host. |
