## 7. File operations

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-113 | Copy and Paste | ⌘C copies the selection to the pasteboard as file URLs (and names for text targets); ⌘V pastes into the current folder, never into a right-clicked folder; "Paste 3 Items" shows the count. | Partial (F-051; B-036 stale internal clipboard wins; B-106 web URLs treated as files) | P0 | M | `NSPasteboard.general` with `NSURL` objects, `changeCount`, `readObjects(forClasses:options: [.urlReadingFileURLsOnly: true])` | Ops, UI | 01-architecture §7.7 clipboard transaction: the pasteboard is the truth, Helm metadata is keyed by `changeCount`. |
| P-114 | Move pasted items | Finder has no Cut for files; ⌥⌘V "Move Items Here" moves what was copied. Helm's ⌘X then ⌘V moves. | Partial (F-051; B-037 cut state consumed before the move succeeds) | P0 | S | Pasteboard flag plus ⌥⌘V menu item | Ops, UI | Keep Helm's Cut (identity); add ⌥⌘V as an alias so copied items can also be moved. Cut state must survive a failed move. |
| P-115 | Cut items dimmed | Not a Finder feature (Nautilus and Windows do it). | No | P1 | S | Snapshot flag per `ItemID` | UI | Helm extra that makes its Cut semantics visible. |
| P-116 | Duplicate | ⌘D makes "X copy", "X copy 2" in the same folder, preserving metadata; on APFS it clones (instant). Localized suffix. | No (Duplicate unbound; Helm's ⌘D is Star, P-076) | P0 | S | `FileManager.copyItem` (uses `clonefile` on APFS when possible) or `copyfile(3)` with `COPYFILE_CLONE` | Ops, Core | Name generation is pure logic in Core (`NameGenerator`): "X copy", "X copy 2", "X 2" for conflicts on move/copy into another folder. |
| P-117 | Conflict naming | Pasting or duplicating in the same folder yields "X copy", then "X copy 2"; "Keep Both" in the conflict dialog for a different folder yields "X 2" `[Needs verification on macOS]` for the exact suffix in each case. Helm always uses "X 2" (F-052; B-116 breaks `a.tar.gz`). | Partial | P0 | S | `NameGenerator` with multi-part extension awareness | Core | Decide one rule and document it: same-folder duplicate gets " copy", cross-folder keep-both gets " 2". Handle `.tar.gz` by a known compound-extension list. |
| P-118 | Move vs copy default | Dragging within a volume moves; across volumes copies; ⌘-drag forces a move; ⌥-drag forces a copy; ⌥⌘-drag makes an alias; the cursor shows a + or ↩ badge. | Partial (B-045: Option toggles copy, always move otherwise, global flag read at validate and accept) | P0 | M | `NSDraggingInfo.draggingSourceOperationMask`, `volumeIdentifierKey` comparison, `NSDraggingSession` | Ops, UI | 01-architecture Q5 default is Finder parity with a setting. The operation chosen at validate must be the one executed. |
| P-119 | Conflict dialog | "An item named X already exists in this location. Do you want to replace it with the one you're moving?" with Keep Both, Stop, Replace, Skip (for multiple), "Apply to all", and newer/older/same-date hints. Folder onto folder: Replace deletes the destination folder (not merge); Merge appears only when ⌥-dragging a folder. | No (silent suffixing, F-052) | P0 | L | Own `NSAlert`/sheet driven by `OperationPlanner` conflicts | Ops, UI, Core | Replace-folder is a known Finder data-loss trap; Helm should default Replace-on-folder to Merge with "Replace entirely" as an explicit choice. Plan first, ask once, then execute (01-architecture §7.3). |
| P-120 | Progress window | One "Copy"/"Move" window listing operations with a bar, item and byte counts, time remaining, a stop button per operation, "Preparing to copy…" while enumerating; completion plays no sound but the window closes. | No (F-061 view exists unhosted; B-049) | P0 | L | Own `NSPanel` fed by `OperationProgress`; `NSProgress` optional for the Dock | UI, Ops | Byte progress needs a copy loop with callbacks: `copyfile(3)` with `copyfile_state_set(COPYFILE_STATE_STATUS_CB)` or chunked `FileHandle` I/O. `FileManager.copyItem` reports nothing. |
| P-121 | Cancel semantics | Stop removes the partially copied item; a move is never left half-done (the source stays until the copy is verified). | No | P0 | M | Cancellation checked per item and per chunk | Ops | Cross-volume move is copy-verify-delete (01-architecture §14.2 verifies by size). |
| P-122 | Copy fidelity | Extended attributes, resource forks, ACLs, flags, dates, tags, comments and quarantine survive copies; APFS clones within a volume; sparse files stay sparse. | Partial (`FileManager.copyItem` preserves xattrs and forks; no clone control; sparse `[Needs verification on macOS]`) | P0 | M | `copyfile(3)` with `COPYFILE_ALL | COPYFILE_CLONE | COPYFILE_DATA_SPARSE`, `clonefile(2)` | FS, Ops | Wrap the C calls once in `HelmFileSystem` behind `#if canImport(Darwin)`; keep a Foundation fallback for the in-memory fake. |
| P-123 | Hard links | Finder never creates them; copying a hard-linked file yields an independent copy. | n/a | P2 | S | `FileManager.linkItem` if ever exposed | Ops | Do not expose; note only. |
| P-124 | Symbolic links | Shown with an alias badge; opening follows the link; a symlink to a folder navigates; copying copies the link itself; dangling links are shown and can be trashed. | Partial (B-071 symlinked folders open in another app; F-069) | P0 | S | `isSymbolicLinkKey`, `destinationOfSymbolicLink`, `URL.resolvingSymlinksInPath` | FS, Core | Decide identity: navigate to the link path (so Back works) but list the target. |
| P-125 | Aliases | ⌃⌘A "Make Alias" creates "X alias" beside the original; ⌥⌘-drag creates one at the drop target; opening resolves (even after the original moved); a broken alias offers Fix Alias / Delete Alias; ⌘R shows the original. | No | P1 | M | `URL.bookmarkData(options: .suitableForBookmarkFile, …)`, `URL.writeBookmarkData(_:to:)`, `URL(resolvingAliasFileAt:options:)`, `isAliasFileKey` | FS, Ops, UI | Alias creation on a network or FAT volume still works (bookmark data is a regular file). Keep symlink creation out of the menu as Finder does; 01-architecture lists the command seam. |
| P-126 | Move to Trash and Put Back | ⌘⌫ moves to the volume's trash (`~/.Trash`, `/Volumes/X/.Trashes/<uid>`, iCloud trash); Put Back returns an item to its original folder; dragging to the Dock Trash does the same. | Partial (F-053; B-087 single-volume view; no Put Back; B-109 Trash unreadable without Full Disk Access) | P0 | M | `FileManager.trashItem(at:resultingItemURL:)`, own journal of (trashed URL, origin) for Put Back | Ops, FS, Persist | Finder records origins in the Trash folder's `.DS_Store`, which Helm cannot read; Put Back works only for items Helm trashed (01-architecture §7.8). Say so in the UI. |
| P-127 | Empty Trash | ⇧⌘⌫ with a confirmation naming the count; ⌥⇧⌘⌫ skips the prompt; empties every volume's trash; items in use are reported; "Remove items after 30 days" is a setting. | No | P0 | M | No public API; enumerate and delete the trash directories; requires Full Disk Access | Ops, FS | AppleScript `tell application "Finder" to empty` is the only Finder-driven route and needs Automation consent and a running Finder; acceptable as an optional fallback, not the default. |
| P-128 | Delete Immediately | ⌥⌘⌫ or context "Delete Immediately…" removes without the Trash after a confirmation. | No (F-060 dead `deleteItems`) | P0 | S | `FileManager.removeItem` behind a confirmed command | Ops, UI | Never callable from undo (B-041). |
| P-129 | Locked item handling | Trashing or renaming a locked item asks to unlock and continue. | No | P1 | S | `isUserImmutable` check in preflight, clear flag on consent | Ops, UI | |
| P-130 | Privileged operations | Modifying items you do not own prompts "Finder wants to make changes" and runs as root. | No | P2 | XL | Only `SMAppService` daemon + XPC (macOS 13) or `osascript "do shell script … with administrator privileges"` | App, Ops | Recommend the error path plus an "Open in Terminal" hint; a privileged helper is a security surface a blind build should not create. |
| P-131 | Items in use | "The operation can't be completed because X is in use" with Skip/Stop; moving an open file across volumes is refused. | No | P1 | S | `EBUSY`/`ETXTBSY` mapping in the executor | Ops | |
| P-132 | New Folder | ⇧⌘N creates "untitled folder" ("untitled folder 2"…) and starts inline rename; in a search view it is disabled. | Partial (F-056 creates "New Folder" immediately, no rename; B-031 wrong target in Recent) | P0 | S | Create then dispatch rename | Ops, UI | 01-architecture Q2: immediate creation followed by inline rename; keep Helm's "New Folder" name. |
| P-133 | New Folder with Selection | ⌃⌘N creates "New Folder With Items", moves the selection into it, and starts rename. | No | P1 | S | Planner: create + move as one undoable command | Ops, UI | |
| P-134 | New file from template | Helm: `~/Templates` plus Empty Text File (Nautilus). Finder: none (Stationery only). | Yes (F-057; B-031 target in virtual locations) | P0 | S | `TemplateProvider` | FS, Ops | Keep; name the created file after the template and start inline rename. |
| P-135 | Filename validation | Refuses empty, `.` / `..`, names containing `/` (Finder maps `:`), warns on a leading dot (hidden), limits to the volume's name length, strips trailing whitespace, warns when the extension changes (P-363). | No (B-046 raw path components; batch rename unvalidated) | P0 | S | `FileNameValidator` in Core; `NAME_MAX` / `pathconf(_PC_NAME_MAX)` for the limit | Core, Ops | APFS limits names to 255 UTF-8 bytes; HFS+ to 255 UTF-16 units; use `pathconf` at the destination `[Needs verification on macOS]` for exotic volumes. |
| P-136 | Batch rename | "Rename N Items…": Replace Text (find/replace), Add Text (before/after name), Format (Name and Index, Name and Counter, Name and Date; custom format, start number), live preview of the first few, conflicts refused. | Partial (F-055 three modes with tokens; B-047 no conflict or swap planning) | P0 | M | `BatchRenamePlanner` in Core producing one journaled command | Core, Ops, UI | Keep Helm's token syntax; add Finder's Format options as presets. Use temporary names for swaps. |
| P-137 | Undo for every entry point | Drag-and-drop, paste, menu, batch rename and duplicate are all undoable as single steps; redo exists. | Partial (B-044 drops skip undo; per-item batch undo) | P0 | M | All mutations through `OperationExecutor` | Ops, UI | |
| P-138 | Operations outlive the view | Closing the tab or window does not cancel a copy; the progress window persists; undo targets are not freed objects. | No (B-049, B-100, B-105) | P0 | M | App-scoped `OperationJournal` and executor | Ops, App | |
| P-139 | Partial failure | With many items, a failure reports the item and offers Skip / Retry / Stop; completed items stay done and are undoable; the UI refreshes every touched folder. | No (B-038 first failure aborts, no result) | P0 | M | Per-item results in the journal | Ops, UI | |
| P-140 | Preflight | Moving a folder into itself or a descendant, dropping onto its own parent, or selecting an ancestor with its descendants is refused or treated as a no-op. | No (B-040 same-folder drop renames) | P0 | S | `OperationPlanner` checks on standardized paths | Ops, Core | Linux-testable. |
| P-141 | Cross-volume move | Copy, verify, then delete the source; on failure the source is untouched. | No | P0 | M | Executor plan | Ops | Verify by size (and optionally by `copyfile` return) before deleting. |
| P-142 | Space check | "There isn't enough space" before starting when the destination lacks room. | No | P1 | S | `volumeAvailableCapacityForImportantUsageKey` versus planned bytes | Ops | Clones on APFS need no space; skip the check for same-volume clones. |
