## 8. Compress and expand

| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-156 | Compress | "Compress X" makes `X.zip` beside it; several items make `Archive.zip`; progress is shown; resource forks and xattrs go into `__MACOSX`; conflicts become `Archive 2.zip`. | No | P1 | M | `/usr/bin/ditto -c -k --sequesterRsrc --keepParent` through `Process`; or libarchive (`archive.h` ships in the macOS SDK `[Needs verification on macOS]`) | Ops, FS | `ditto` is what Archive Utility uses and is always present; `Process` is public and simple. Run on the I/O executor, surface progress by output size. |
| P-157 | Expand | Double-clicking an archive expands it with Archive Utility next to it (Archive Utility's own preference decides whether to keep the archive). | Yes (`NSWorkspace.open` dispatches to Archive Utility) | P0 | S | `NSWorkspace.open` | UI | Nothing to build. |
| P-158 | Expand here for other formats | Archive Utility handles zip, tar, gz, bz2, xz, cpio, xar; not 7z or rar. | No | P2 | M | `/usr/bin/tar -xf` (libarchive-based; handles zip, xz, bzip2, zstd on macOS 13+ `[Needs verification on macOS]`) | Ops | A Helm "Expand Here" command with a format whitelist; 7z/rar need third-party tools, out of scope. |
| P-159 | Encrypted archives | Archive Utility prompts for a password on expansion; Finder cannot create encrypted zips. | No | P2 | M | `/usr/bin/zip -e` and `/usr/bin/unzip -P` through `Process` with the password passed on stdin, never argv | Ops | Password in argv is visible in `ps`; use `-P` only via a pipe or prefer `ditto` which cannot encrypt. |
| P-160 | Archive progress and cancel | Compress shows progress and can be stopped; the partial archive is removed. | No | P1 | S | `Process.terminate()`, cleanup | Ops, UI | Reuse the operations panel (P-120). |

