| ID | Item | What Finder does | Helm today | Pri | Cx | APIs | Modules | Notes / pitfalls |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| P-161 | Assign tags | Context menu shows seven colour dots plus "Tags…"; Get Info and the toolbar Tags item open a token editor; dragging an item onto a sidebar tag assigns it. | No | P1 | M | `URLResourceValues.tagNames` (read-write, public) | FS, UI | Writing `tagNames` sets the xattr and keeps the legacy label in sync `[Needs verification on macOS]` for the legacy `FinderInfo` label bits. |
| P-162 | Storage format | Tags live in the xattr `com.apple.metadata:_kMDItemUserTags` as a binary plist array of `"Name\n<colourIndex>"` strings; the legacy colour label is the `FinderInfo` label bits, exposed as `labelNumberKey`. | No | P1 | S | `tagNamesKey`, `labelNumberKey` (read-write); raw `getxattr`/`setxattr` only when a colour must be set for a custom name | FS | Custom tag colours are not expressible through `tagNames` (names only); write the raw xattr for those. Keep the raw format in one `HelmFileSystem.TagCodec` with Linux tests on the plist bytes. |
| P-163 | Tag list and colours | Finder keeps the tag list (names, colours, order, favourites) in its own synced preferences. | No | P1 | M | `NSWorkspace.shared.fileLabels` / `fileLabelColors` for the seven standard labels; own `TagStore` for custom tags discovered from files | Persist, UI | Finder's tag dictionary file (`~/Library/SyncedPreferences/com.apple.finder.plist`) is a private, synced store; read it best-effort for colours of custom tags, never write it. |
| P-164 | Tag dots and search | Views show up to three colour dots after the name; Spotlight searches by `kMDItemUserTags`. | No | P1 | M | Snapshot includes tag names; `NSMetadataQuery` predicate on `kMDItemUserTags` | Core, Search, UI | Add `tagNamesKey` to the prefetch set only when tags are enabled; it is cheap but not free on network volumes. |
| P-165 | Sidebar Tags section | Lists tags with colour; clicking shows every tagged item (a Spotlight query); "Recent Tags" option; drag onto a tag assigns. | No | P2 | M | Virtual `Location.tag(name)` backed by `HelmSearch` | Core, Search, UI | Needs the virtual-location model and P-161. |
| P-166 | Tag editor sheet | "Tags…" opens a small popover with a token field and suggestions. | No | P1 | S | `NSTokenField` or SwiftUI `TextField` with suggestions | UI | |
| P-167 | Rename or delete a tag globally | Finder Settings > Tags renames or deletes a tag and re-tags every file. | No | P2 | L | Spotlight query for `kMDItemUserTags == name` then rewrite each file's tags | Search, FS | Slow and unindexed volumes are missed; show a count and confirm. |
| P-168 | Stars versus tags | Finder has no stars; Favourite tags are the nearest thing. Helm's Starred is a JSON set keyed by path. | Partial (F-029; B-027 duplicated stores; B-113 unstable order) | P1 | M | `StarStore` protocol with a tag-backed implementation ("Starred" tag) | Persist, FS | 01-architecture Q7 keeps JSON; a tag-backed store would let stars survive moves and show in Finder. Offer it as a setting once tags exist. |
| P-169 | Tag colours accessibility | Differentiate Without Colour shows shapes or names instead of dots. | No | P2 | S | `NSWorkspace.accessibilityDisplayShouldDifferentiateWithoutColor` | UI | |

