| P-172 | Search tokens | Typed filters become tokens: `kind:image`, `date:yesterday`, `modified:>1/1/24`, `created:`, `tag:`, `author:`, `from:`; a suggestion popup lists them. | No | P1 | M | `SpotlightQueryBuilder` in `HelmSearch` mapping tokens to `kMDItemContentTypeTree`, `kMDItemContentModificationDate`, `kMDItemUserTags` | Search, Core, UI | Pure parsing is Linux-testable. Date language parsing is the long tail; support a fixed grammar. |
| P-173 | Criteria rows | The + button adds rows: Kind, Last opened, Last modified, Created, Name, Contents, Other… (any attribute), with Any/All; "System files" and "Hidden" criteria. | No | P1 | L | Same builder; `MDItemCopyAttributeNames` for Other… | Search, UI | Build after tokens; both compile to one predicate. |
| P-174 | Save as Smart Folder | "Save" writes a `.savedSearch` plist (keys `RawQuery`, `RawQueryDict` with `SearchScopes` and `SearchCriteria`, `CompatibleVersion`) to `~/Library/Saved Searches`, optionally adding it to the sidebar. | No | P1 | M | Plist encoding with `PropertyListSerialization`; `NSPredicate(fromMetadataQueryString:)` to reload | Search, Persist | Write `RawQuery` and `SearchScopes` only; `SearchCriteria` is Finder's private UI state and may be omitted `[Needs verification on macOS]` that Finder opens a `.savedSearch` without it. |
| P-175 | Open smart folders | Double-clicking a `.savedSearch` (Finder's or Helm's) shows live results as a location. | No | P1 | M | Read `RawQuery` and scopes, run through `SearchService` | Search, Core, UI | Register `com.apple.finder.smart-folder` as an Alternate Viewer in Info.plist. |
| P-176 | Result location | Each result shows its enclosing folder (list column or path bar for the selection); ⌘R reveals it. | Partial (M-24 names only) | P0 | S | Parent path in the snapshot; `Location` column | Core, UI | |
| P-177 | Live results | Results update as Spotlight indexes (gathering then updates). | Partial (F-046 observes `DidUpdate`) | P1 | S | `NSMetadataQueryDidUpdate` with `disableUpdates()` while reading | Search | |
| P-178 | Result order | Spotlight relevance by default; any column sort when chosen. | Partial (F-045 own ranking, destroyed by directory sort B-022) | P0 | S | Relevance as a sort key in the snapshot | Core, Search | Keep Helm's ranking table as the relevance order. |
| P-179 | Unindexed locations | Finder falls back silently to a slow enumeration search on volumes without an index and shows "Indexing…" when Spotlight is busy. | No (B-099 silent empty results) | P1 | M | `EnumerationSearchService` (01-architecture) over `DirectoryEnumerator`; `mdutil -s` status is CLI-only | Search, FS | Detect "no results and the scope has no index" by checking `kMDItemFSName` of the folder itself returns nothing; state it in the UI. |
| P-180 | System file exclusion | System files are excluded unless a criterion includes them. | Partial (F-044 path exclusions; C-20 `kMDItemPath` predicates may be ignored) | P1 | S | Post-filter on result paths instead of predicate | Search | 01-architecture §14.2 already avoids `kMDItemPath`. |
| P-181 | Spotlight privacy | Folders excluded in Spotlight privacy settings never appear. | Yes (automatic) | P0 | S | None | — | Combined with P-179 the user can still search them by enumeration. |
| P-182 | Search inside virtual locations | Searching from Recents or Trash searches This Mac or that folder respectively. | Partial (Recent searches everywhere) | P2 | S | Scope from the `Location` | Search, Core | |
| P-183 | Query lifecycle | New keystrokes cancel the previous query; stale results never land; the first results appear quickly. | Partial (B-021 latent cancel, B-023 stale results) | P0 | S | Query generation tokens | Search, Core | |
