| P-255 | Toggle hidden files | ⇧⌘. toggles globally (`AppleShowAllFiles`), applies to every window immediately, persists. | Partial (F-042 ⌘. per tab; not applied to expanded children, completions, Recent; no checkmark) | P0 | S | One setting observed by every snapshot builder; add ⇧⌘. as an alias of ⌘. | Core, Persist, UI | Keep ⌘. (identity) and add ⇧⌘. for muscle memory. Write `AppleShowAllFiles` into Finder's domain? No: do not write other apps' defaults. |
| P-256 | What counts as hidden | Names starting with `.`, the `UF_HIDDEN` flag (`chflags hidden`), the FinderInfo invisible bit; some system paths are hidden by flag (`/bin`, `/usr`, `~/Library`); the legacy `/.hidden` list. | Yes (`isHiddenKey` covers the dot, flag and FinderInfo cases, F-042) | P0 | S | `URLResourceKey.isHiddenKey` | FS | Whether current Finder still honours `/.hidden` `[Needs verification on macOS]`; treat it as unsupported. |
