| P-258 | Show Library Folder | View Options on the home folder has "Show Library Folder", which clears the hidden flag on `~/Library`. | No | P1 | S | `URLResourceValues.isHidden` (settable) on `~/Library` | FS, UI | Also offer "Go to Library" (⌥ in Go menu, P-010) which needs no flag change. |
| P-259 | Show Package Contents | Context item on bundles navigates inside; bundles otherwise behave as files (open, not navigate). | Partial (`isPackage` respected for open; no command) | P0 | S | Navigate with a `showPackageContents` flag so the breadcrumb and Up work inside | UI, Core | Inside a package, hidden-file rules still apply. |
| P-260 | Show all filename extensions | Advanced setting that ignores per-file hidden extensions. | No | P1 | S | Setting consulted by display-name logic (P-152) | Core, Persist | |
| P-261 | Hidden rule everywhere | The hidden setting applies to expanded children, path completion, search results, Recents and Trash. | Partial (F-042 gaps; completion always filters hidden) | P0 | S | Single filter in `PresentationSnapshot` building and `CompletionProvider` | Core, FS | Typing a dot-prefixed path in the address bar must still complete hidden names (Finder's Go to Folder does). |

