| P-269 | Drag source | Writes `public.file-url` for each item (AppKit bridges the legacy `NSFilenamesPboardType`), drags a stack of icons with a count badge, advertises copy, move and link. | Partial (F-067 `NSURL` writers; external mask copy-only; no custom image) | P0 | S | `NSCollectionView.draggingImageForItems`, `NSDraggingItem.imageComponentsProvider`, `draggingSession(_:sourceOperationMaskFor:)` returning `[.copy, .move, .link]` for both contexts | UI | Finder as a destination performs the move itself when it negotiates `.move`; Helm must not delete the source on `draggingSession(_:endedAt:operation:)`. |
| P-270 | Drag destination from other apps | Accepts file URLs from any app with the same modifier semantics; the operation offered is the intersection of the source mask and the modifiers. | Partial (F-067; B-045 ignores the source mask) | P0 | S | `draggingUpdated(_:)` computing the operation once and storing it for `performDragOperation` | UI, Ops | |
| P-271 | File promises | Accepts promised files (images from Safari, Mail attachments, Photos exports) by letting the source write into the folder. | No | P1 | M | `NSFilePromiseReceiver`, `receivePromisedFiles(atDestination:options:operationQueue:reader:)`, register `NSFilePromiseReceiver.readableDraggedTypes` | UI, Ops | The written files appear through the monitor; select them when they arrive. |
| P-272 | Clippings | Dropping text creates `X.textClipping`; dropping a URL creates `X.webloc`; dropping an image creates a picture file. | No | P2 | M | `.webloc` is a plist with a `URL` key (easy); `.textClipping` stores its text in a resource fork (private layout); images via `NSImage` to `CGImageDestination` | Ops | Do `.webloc` and images; skip `.textClipping` or write it as `.txt`. |
| P-273 | Spring-loaded folders | Hovering a drag over a folder, sidebar item, breadcrumb segment or tab opens it after the system delay; pressing Space springs immediately; the drag continues inside. | No | P1 | M | Timer in `draggingUpdated`; the delay comes from System Settings > Accessibility > Pointer Control (`com.apple.springing.delay` in the global domain `[Needs verification on macOS]`) | UI | Navigation during a drag must not reset the drag session; the destination view changes under the cursor. |
| P-274 | Live modifier feedback | Holding ⌥ or ⌘ during a drag updates the cursor badge (+, ↩, alias) and the operation immediately. | Partial (B-045 reads flags at validate and accept; may differ) | P0 | M | `draggingUpdated` is called on modifier change; return the new `NSDragOperation` | UI | |
| P-275 | Drag to Dock and other apps | Items dropped on the Dock Trash are trashed by the Dock; on Dock apps they open; on other windows they copy. | Yes (system behaviour over file URLs) | P0 | S | None beyond P-269 | — | |
| P-276 | Drop on Helm's Dock icon | Opens the folder (or the file's folder) in Helm. | Partial (F-002 first window, not key; B-103) | P0 | S | `application(_:open:)` | App | |
| P-277 | Drops in virtual locations | Dropping into Trash trashes; into search results or Recents is refused. | No (B-031 wrong target) | P1 | S | `DropPlanner` consults the `Location` kind | Ops, Core | |
| P-278 | Drag threshold and selection | Dragging a selected item drags the whole selection; a small movement does not start a drag; a drag on an unselected item selects it first. | Yes (native widgets) | P0 | S | None | — | B-040's "tiny drag renames" is a planner bug, not a threshold one. |
| P-279 | Auto-scroll and expand on hover | Dragging near an edge scrolls; hovering a list folder expands it. | Partial (native auto-scroll) | P1 | S | `NSOutlineView` expands on hover with `draggingUpdated` proposals | UI | |
| P-280 | Drag image formation | Finder shows a stacked pile that fans into a list of icons. | No | P2 | S | `NSDraggingSession.draggingFormation = .stack` | UI | |
| P-281 | Copy also writes names | Copying files then pasting into a text field pastes the file names (not paths). | No | P1 | S | Add `public.utf8-plain-text` with names alongside the URLs | UI | ⌥⌘C (P-294) is the paths variant. |

